@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+# `aarch64-unknown-minixrs`
+
+**Tier: 3**
+
+[minixrs](https://github.com/minixrs) is a microkernel operating system written
+in Rust, with a POSIX userland provided by a fork of musl.
+
+## Target maintainers
+
+[@KevinBarnard](https://github.com/KevinBarnard)
+
+## Requirements
+
+This target is cross-compiled. It needs the minixrs SDK: an LLVM that knows the
+`aarch64-unknown-minixrs` triple, and a musl sysroot for it.
+
+Programs are statically linked `ET_EXEC` images; minixrs has no dynamic loader.
+`panic = "abort"` is the only panic strategy, because no unwinder is linked yet,
+and backtraces are reported as unsupported. Calls the kernel does not implement
+yet fail at run time with `ENOSYS`.
+
+The linker is `aarch64-unknown-minixrs-clang`, the SDK's clang under its
+triple-prefixed name, which must be on `PATH`.
+
+## Building the target
+
+Against the SDK's LLVM:
+
+```toml
+[build]
+target = ["aarch64-apple-darwin", "aarch64-unknown-minixrs"]
+
+[target.aarch64-apple-darwin]
+llvm-config = "<sdk>/bin/llvm-config"
+
+[target.aarch64-unknown-minixrs]
+cc = "<sdk>/bin/aarch64-unknown-minixrs-clang"
+ar = "<sdk>/bin/llvm-ar"
+ranlib = "<sdk>/bin/llvm-ranlib"
+linker = "<sdk>/bin/aarch64-unknown-minixrs-clang"
+```
+
+```sh
+./x build --stage 1 library
+```
+
+## Building Rust programs
+
+```sh
+cargo +minixrs build --target aarch64-unknown-minixrs
+```
+
+## Testing
+
+There is no test runner for this target.
+
+## Cross-compilation toolchains and C code
+
+C code is compiled with the SDK's clang, `--target=aarch64-unknown-minixrs`.
